          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Evaluating it gives "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 6 } { 7 6 8 0 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.126,
            0.58,
            0.147
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Upon simplifying to its lowest form, we get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.434,
            0.158,
            0.563,
            0.193
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_21_equation_4.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{6}{7680} = \\frac{1}{1280}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.191,
            0.593,
            0.21
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, one cowrie shell was given to the beggar."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.209,
            0.847,
            0.247
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You can see in the answer Bhāskarāchārya’s humour! The miser had given the beggar only one coin of the least value (cowrie)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.247,
            0.849,
            0.375
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Around the 12th century, several types of coins were in use in different kingdoms of the Indian subcontinent. Most commonly used were gold coins (called dinars/gadyanas and hunas), silver coins (called drammas/tankas), copper coins (called kasus/panas and mashakas), and cowrie shells. The exact conversion rates between these coins varied depending on the region, time period, economic conditions, weights of coins and their purity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.375,
            0.848,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Gold coins had high-value and were used in large transactions and to store wealth. Silver coins were more commonly used in everyday transactions. Copper coins had low-value and were used in smaller transactions. Cowrie shells were the lowest denomination and were used in very small transactions and as change."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.467,
            0.848,
            0.506
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If we assume 1 gold dinar = 12 silver drammas, 1 silver dramma = 4 copper panas, 1 copper pana = 6 mashakas, and 1 pana = 30 cowrie shells,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.311,
            0.513,
            0.688,
            0.553
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_21_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "1\\ \\mathrm{copper\\ pan}a = \\frac{1}{48}\\ \\mathrm{gold\\ dina}\\left(\\frac{1}{12} \\times \\frac{1}{4}\\right)"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.33,
            0.56,
            0.669,
            0.583
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_21_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "1. { \\mathrm { c o w r i e ~ s h e l l } } = { \\mathrm { \\bar { \\mathrm { ~ \\text-- ~ } } } } { \\mathrm { c o p p e r ~ p a n a s } }"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.343,
            0.596,
            0.653,
            0.617
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_21_equation_12.jpg",
